Sure!  Loops allow you to repeat a set of instructions multiple times.  In C, there are three types of loops:   for { Start Number To End Number } { Expression } { Increment/Decrement }  For example, here’s a loop to print the first 10 odd numbers: 

for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    printf("%d ", i);
}

Here’s a more complex example:  There’s a set of numbers that you want to print, but you only want to print some of them.  To do this, you use the following loop to print the first seven numbers from a set of numbers that you’re interested in:

for (int i = 0; i < 7; i++) {
    printf("%d ", numbers[i]);
}

In the example above, “0” is the start number (you start at 0, not 1), “7” is the end number, and the expression “numbers[i]” is the number that you want to print.  Note that the index is 0-based in C.

